  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of forums on key topics to promote political dialogue are organised between civil society, elected assemblies (NARS; LAs) and other stakeholders
2. NARS and LA committees are conducting a draft law review or oversight inquiry based on an evidence-based gender impact assessment.
3. Percentage of leadership posts within elected assemblies (NARS; LAs) held by women.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 1
2.  0
3. 10 %</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	30% of leadership posts within elected assemblies (NARS; LAs) held by women.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.  After 2020 general elections significant number of local assemblies appointed women at the position of secretaries (over 50%) with limited number of female candidates appointed as speakers (15%). Among NARS officials there are only two women as deputy speakers (out of 6 deputy speakers in total, 20%).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 3 forums for political dialogue organized between civil society, elected assemblies (NARS; LAs) and other stakeholders.
2. 4 gender impact assessments included in draft law scrutiny and oversight inquiries by elected assemblies (NARS; LAs).
3. 20% of leadership posts within elected assemblies (NARS; LAs) held by women</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 3 events in total organized - 2 preparatory workshops with CSOs and one forum for political dialogue in Zajecar
2. Two field visits of the WPN organized with the workshops at the local level to perform oversight over the LSGs obligations in implementing the Law on Gender Equaiity
3. 50% of local assemblies secretaries are women, as well as the 15% of the speakers</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 4 forums for political dialogue organized between civil society, elected assemblies (NARS; LAs) and other stakeholders.
2. 5 gender impact assessments included in draft law scrutiny and oversight inquiries by elected assemblies (NARS; LAs).
3. 25% of leadership posts within elected assemblies (NARS; LAs) held by women</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
